! The `ph.x` input that generated `reference.out.ph-al4-metal`, from the ground
! state of `al4-metal.in`:
!
!   pw.x -in al4-metal.in && ph.x -in al4-metal.ph.in
!
! `outdir` and `fildyn` are rewritten by whoever regenerates it. `ph.x` splits
! the twelve modes into four irreducible representations of three here, and its
! `Fermi energy shift` prints as 1e-25 -- this cell's modes move no charge, so
! `ef_shift` is inactive and is *not* what this case tests.
Al4 Gamma phonons
 &inputph
  prefix='al4',
  outdir='OUTDIR/tmp',
  tr2_ph=1.0d-14,
  fildyn='OUTDIR/al4.dynG',
 /
0.0 0.0 0.0
